\ulnone\b0\fs24 DALL\'b7E is a generative AI model developed by OpenAI that creates images from text descriptions. Users simply provide a prompt, and the model generates corresponding images. DALL\'b7E combines natural language understanding with image generation capabilities. \par
\b How DALL\'b7E Works\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent360\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\b0 User enters a text prompt.\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}The model understands objects, relationships, colors, and styles.\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}AI generates one or more matching images.\par
{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}Images can be edited or refined through additional prompts.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qj\par
\ul\b\fs28 Codex\par
\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\qc\kerning0\ulnone\b0\f2\fs22\lang9 }\kerning2\ul\b\f0\fs28\lang16393\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj\ulnone\b0\fs24 Codex is an AI model developed by OpenAI specifically for programming and software development. It translates natural language instructions into executable code and forms the foundation of AI coding assistants such as GitHub Copilot. \par
\b How Codex Works\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent360\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj\b0 User provides a programming instruction.\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}Codex understands the desired functionality.\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}It generates code in the required programming language.\par
{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}Developers can edit or execute the generated code.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj\ul\b\fs28\par
Stable Diffusion\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qc\kerning0\ulnone\b0\f2\fs22\lang9 }\kerning2\ul\b\f0\fs28\lang16393\par
\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj\ulnone\b0\fs24 Stable Diffusion is an open-source text-to-image generation model developed by Stability AI and research collaborators. It uses diffusion techniques to generate high-quality images from text prompts. Unlike many proprietary models, Stable Diffusion can be run locally on personal computers and customized for specific applications.\par
\b How Stable Diffusion Works\par
Step 1: Text Input\par
\b0 The user enters a prompt.\par
\b Example:\b0\par
"A lion wearing a crown sitting on a throne"\par
\b Step 2: Noise Creation\par
\b0 The model starts with random noise.\par
\b Step 3: Denoising Process\par
\b0 Using neural networks, noise is gradually removed while aligning the image with the text description.\par
\b Step 4: Image Generation\par
\b0 A realistic image matching the prompt is produced.\par
\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qc\ul\b\fs56 Diffusion\par
