\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj\ulnone\b0\fs24 A \b Diffusion Model\b0  is a type of generative AI model that creates images by starting with random noise and gradually removing that noise until a meaningful image appears. This process is inspired by the way particles diffuse in physics.\par
\b How Diffusion Works\par
Step 1: Forward Process\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj Noise is gradually added to a training image.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}After many steps, the image becomes pure random noise.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj\b Step 2: Reverse Process\b0\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj The AI learns how to reverse the noise addition process.\par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}It removes noise step by step to create a new image.\par

