\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl360\slmult1\qj\ulnone\fs24 Transformers\b0  are a type of deep learning architecture introduced in 2017 that revolutionized Natural Language Processing (NLP). They are the foundation of modern AI models such as \b GPT, ChatGPT, BERT, Gemini, Claude, and LLaMA\b0 . Transformers use a mechanism called \b Self-Attention\b0  to understand the relationships between words in a sentence, regardless of their positions.\par
Unlike older models such as Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs), Transformers can process all words in a sentence simultaneously, making them faster and more efficient. This ability allows them to capture context more accurately and handle large amounts of data.\par
\b Key Components of a Transformer\par
1. Encoder: \b0 The encoder receives the input text and converts it into meaningful numerical representations. Multiple encoder layers help the model understand the context of the input.\b\par
2. Self-Attention Mechanism: \b0 Self-attention allows the model to determine which words in a sentence are most important when understanding a particular word. For example:\b\par
Sentence:\b0  "The cat sat on the mat because it was comfortable."\par
The Transformer understands that \b "it"\b0  refers to \b "the mat"\b0  rather than \b "the cat."\b0\par
\b 3. Decoder: \b0 The decoder generates the output by using the information processed by the encoder and predicting the next word or token.\b\par
\b0\par

